\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come, my soul, thou must be waking,
\par Now is breaking
\par O'er the earth another day;
\par Come to him who made this splendour,
\par See thou render
\par All thy feeble strength can pay.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Gladly hail the sun returning;
\par Ready burning
\par Be the incense of thy powers;
\par For the night is safely ended,
\par God hath tended
\par With His care thy helpless hours.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Pray that He may prosper ever
\par Each endeavour,
\par When thine aim is good and true;
\par But that He may ever thwart thee,
\par And convert thee,
\par When thou evil  wouldst pursue.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Think that He thy ways beholdeth,
\par He unfoldeth,
\par Every fault that lurks within;
\par He the hidden shame glossed over
\par Can discover,
\par And discern each deed of sin.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Mayest thou on life's last morrow,
\par Free from sorrow,
\par Pass away in slumber sweet;
\par And, released from death's dark sadness
\par Rise in gladness
\par That far brighter Sun to greet.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Our God's bounteous gifts abuse not,
\par Light refuse not, 
\par But His Spirit's voice obey:
\par Thou with Him shalt dwell, beholding,
\par Light unfolding
\par All things in unclouded day.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

